Step 1 — Create files on GitHub
Inside your repository, create the folder Experiment-03-MNIST-Autoencoder and add all five files above.
Step 2 — Run locally in VS Code
Open a terminal in the experiment folder.

Create and activate a virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv



Windows:

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1



Install dependencies:

python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt



Step 3 — Execute the Autoencoder

python autoencoder.py



On the first run, Keras downloads the MNIST dataset, so an internet connection is required. Training may take several minutes on a CPU.
Step 4 — Verify outputs
Check that the following files exist:
- outputs/reconstructed_images.png
- outputs/training_loss.png
- models/mnist_autoencoder.keras
Replace the illustrative output.txt with your actual terminal results after running the program.
